@startuml gateway_class_diagram

title Gateway Pattern Class Diagram

class APIGateway {
    - base_url: str
    - api_key: str
    - cache: Cache
    - session: Session
    + __init__(base_url: str, api_key: str, cache: Cache): void
    + get(endpoint: str): dict
}

note top of APIGateway
    The Gateway pattern provides a single entry point to a subsystem,
    encapsulating the complexity of interacting with external systems or services.
    It acts as a facade, simplifying the interface for clients and allowing for
    easier maintenance, testing, and changes to the underlying systems.
end note

class Cache {
    - expiration: timedelta
    - location: str
    + {abstract} get(key: str): str
    + {abstract} set(key: str, value: str): void
    + {abstract} is_valid(key: str): bool
}

note right of Cache
    Abstract base class for caching mechanisms.
    Defines the interface for cache operations.
end note

class FileSystemCache {
    - location: str
    + __init__(location: str, *args, **kwargs): void
    + __get_cache_path(key: str): str
    + set(key: str, value: str): void
    + get(key: str): str
    + is_valid(key: str): bool
}

note right of FileSystemCache
    Concrete implementation of Cache using the file system.
    Stores cached data in files with expiration checks.
end note



note right of APIGateway
    Gateway class that handles HTTP requests to an external API.
    Supports caching via the Cache interface.
end note

Cache <|-- FileSystemCache : extends
APIGateway --> Cache : uses

@enduml
